<article class="env-lemma" id="07XU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07XU">Lemma <span data-tag="07XU">98.13.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ and $g : \mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{Z}$ be composable $1$-morphisms of categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. If $f$ and $g$ satisfy (<a href="/tag/07XS" data-tag="07XS">98.13.2.1</a>) so does $g \circ f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows formally from Formal Deformation Theory, Lemma <a href="/tag/06HM" data-tag="06HM">90.8.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>